## External services

| Service     | Role                                                          |
|-------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| OpenRouter  | Hosts DeepSeek Chat (Extractor) and Meta Llama 3.3 70B        |
|             | Instruct (Critic + Consolidator) for the default deployment.  |
| Together AI | Hosts the LoRA fine-tuned Llama 3.1 70B Instruct extractor    |
|             | for the specialized-framework deployment (artifacts under     |
|             | `artifacts/paper_data_v6/benchmarks_ft_70b_test/`).           |

API access to either service requires a paid account. Set the corresponding
API key in `.env` (see `.env.example`).

## Evaluation datasets

| Dataset | Source                                              | License       |
|---------|-----------------------------------------------------|---------------|
| SciREX  | Jain, van Zuylen, Hajishirzi, Beltagy. ACL 2020.    | Apache-2.0    |
|         | https://github.com/allenai/SciREX                    |               |
| TDMSci  | Hou, Mariana, Bonin, Cabrio, Villata. ACL 2019.     | Apache-2.0    |
|         | https://github.com/IBM/science-result-extractor      |               |

The datasets themselves are **not redistributed** in this repository. To
reproduce results, follow the dataset-provider's instructions to obtain the
data, then place the SciREX release files under
`data/raw/scirex/scirex_dataset/release_data/{train,dev,test}.jsonl` and the
TDMSci CoNLL files under `data/raw/science-result-extractor/data/TDMSci/conllFormat/`.

The case-study artifact `artifacts/paper_data_v8/deployment_case_study/`
references 100 arXiv papers fetched in 2025-01-01 to 2026-05-31. Only the
framework's extracted ContributionRecord JSONs are released — the source
paper texts can be re-fetched from arXiv via `scripts/v8_fetch_recent.py`.

## Model families

The framework references the following model identifiers via OpenRouter and
Together AI. We hold no rights to these models; they are referenced for
reproducibility only.

- DeepSeek family — DeepSeek Chat (open weights).
- Meta Llama 3.3 70B Instruct (open weights, custom community license).
- Meta Llama 3.1 70B / 8B Instruct Reference (open weights, custom community
  license; used as the base for the fine-tuned specialized extractor).
- OpenAI gpt-4o-2024-11-20 (closed weights; used in the closed-source
  comparison ablation under `artifacts/paper_data_v7/closed_source_comparison/`).
